{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Reproduced on origin/main (worktree at d72c477): infer_provider('gemini-2.5-pro') -> 'google_genai'; 'google_genai' is in neither _pydantic_ai_known_providers() nor ProviderSession._builders (['anthropic','bedrock']); provider_factory raises LLMConfigError. Fix: _PROVIDER_PREFIXES maps gemini -> 'google' (pydantic-ai's current canonical Gemini Developer API name, already a member of KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES and of pydantic-ai's own known names; google-gla/google-vertex resolve but are deprecated and removed in v2.0). Mutation-checked both directions: with the one-line production change reverted the new tests fail 4/119 (test_the_inference_path_is_not_validated, test_every_inferred_provider_name_is_resolvable[gemini], test_a_bare_gemini_id_composes_a_resolvable_target, test_infer_provider); restored, 119 pass. docs/env-vars.md is generated and records config.py line numbers, so the added comment lines required regenerating it (scripts/gen_env_registry.py). Gates: make lint exit 0, make typecheck exit 0."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785708189475740001,"uuid":"c892bad5-b473-4c48-bf83-2e87a788c6f2"}